.TH COND 1 "April 2026" "Conductor Engine" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cond \- minimal orchestration runtime CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cond
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-store\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcond\fR is the command-line interface for Conductor Engine.
It runs tasks, executes workflows, lists capabilities, inspects local task history,
and surfaces component health checks.
.PP
Use \fBman cond\fR for the stable command reference.
Use \fBcond help\fR for runtime-aware help, including capability topics derived from the currently loaded registry.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show argparse usage help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed \fBcond\fR version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-store \fIPATH\fR
Path to the local JSON task store.
Defaults to \fB.conductor/tasks.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to a capability configuration YAML file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B cond run \fITASK\-FILE\fR
Execute one YAML or JSON task file through the supervisor.
.TP
.B cond workflow run \fIWORKFLOW\-FILE\fR
Execute a workflow YAML or JSON file through the planner, worker, supervisor, and validator flow.
.TP
.B cond capability list
List every registered capability with risk level and tags.
.TP
.B cond task list
List tasks saved in the local task store.
Supports \fB\-\-limit\fR, \fB\-\-offset\fR, and \fB\-\-status\fR filters.
.TP
.B cond task show \fITASK\-ID\fR
Show one stored task in detail, including workflow linkage and audit trail.
Accepts a full task id or a unique prefix from the list view.
.TP
.B cond task approve \fITASK\-ID\fR
Approve a task in \fBAWAITING_APPROVAL\fR state.
By default the supervisor immediately resumes execution; use \fB\-\-no\-run\fR to only record approval.
.TP
.B cond task cancel \fITASK\-ID\fR
Cancel a task in \fBAWAITING_APPROVAL\fR state.
.TP
.B cond health
Run \fBhealth_check()\fR across the CLI-facing runtime components.
Returns exit code 0 when healthy and 1 when any issues are reported.
.TP
.B cond snapshot
Emit a versioned JSON control-plane snapshot for tasks, approvals, workflow traces,
capabilities, and component health.
.TP
.B cond help [\fITOPIC\fR]
Show offline dynamic help for commands and capabilities.
Capability help is runtime-aware and remains available here instead of through separate manpages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a basic task:
.EX
cond run examples/echo.yaml
.EE
.TP
Run a workflow:
.EX
cond workflow run examples/workflow-echo.yaml
.EE
.TP
Inspect approval-gated tasks:
.EX
cond task list --status awaiting_approval
.EE
.TP
Approve a task by id prefix:
.EX
cond task approve 4df2c8ab
.EE
.TP
Run health checks:
.EX
cond health
.EE
.TP
Export the Phase 4 bootstrap snapshot:
.EX
cond snapshot
.EE
.TP
Read static CLI reference:
.EX
man cond
.EE
.TP
Read dynamic capability help:
.EX
cond help echo
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cond (1),
.BR cond\ --help ,
and
.B cond help
for runtime-aware capability and plugin topics.
